@startuml 09_research_methodology
' Activity diagram — 6-phase experimental research methodology
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F4F7FB
  BorderColor #4A6FA5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #EAF2E9
  DiamondBorderColor #4A7A45
}
title Research Methodology — Experimental Phases

start

:Phase 1 — Design & Parity;
note right
  Design the microservice architecture.
  Enforce apple-to-apple parity across 4 stacks:
  bcrypt cost 10, DB pool 20, cache TTL 30s,
  CPU 1.0 / 512MB, identical 72-bucket histogram.
end note

:Phase 2 — Load & Metric Collection;
note right
  Generate load with k6.
  Scrape metrics into Prometheus.
  Extract P95 + features via collect.py.
end note

:Phase 3 — Feature Engineering & Training;
note right
  Build lag / rolling / rate / resource features.
  Train and compare 4 models:
  LSTM, GRU (proposed) vs XGBoost, Prophet (baseline).
end note

:Phase 4 — Accuracy Evaluation;
note right
  Chronological train/test split (70/15/15).
  Metrics: RMSE, MAE, sMAPE.
  Recurrent models retrained over **10 seeds**
  -> report mean +/- std, not a single run.
  Significance: Wilcoxon signed-rank across seeds
  + Diebold-Mariano (HLN-corrected) per sample.
  Report aggregate AND per-scenario performance.
end note

:Phase 5 — Deploy & Validate Controller;
note right
  Deploy the hybrid predictive controller
  on Kubernetes.
  Validate proactive UP / robust DOWN scaling.
end note

:Phase 6 — Ablation & Hypothesis Testing;
note right
  Run full ablation:
  4 scenarios x 4 sub-intensities x 4 stacks
  = 64 tests.
  Test hypotheses H1-H4.
end note

:Test Hypotheses;
note right
  H1: Deep learning (LSTM/GRU) forecasts P95
      more accurately than baselines in the
      burst regimes that trigger scale-up.
  H2: Predictive scaling reduces SLO violations
      vs reactive scaling.
  H3: Hybrid UP/DOWN policy outperforms
      forecast-only or reactive-only policies.
  H4: Forecast accuracy and scaling gains
      are consistent across the 4 stacks.
end note

stop

@enduml
